  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Playin' In The Band** (1 review): Calls this Playin' jam full of energy [5]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Big Boss Man**: rare: 10 archived performances [6]\n- **New Minglewood Blues**: rare: 14 archived performances [6]\n- **Case Jones**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [6]\n- **Liberty fake**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [6]\n- **Johnny B Goode**: rare: 13 archived performances [6]\n- Earliest performances in the archive: When I Paint My Masterpiece [6]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **deadandco2016-07-07.akg481** (recommended): source not stated; 19 songs; 183 min; rated 4.75/5 by 4 [1]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Says John Mayer brings a different style to the band, but the Dead have always evolved [2]\n- Set has none of the big segues like Help>Slip>Franklin, St. Stephen>The Eleven or Scarlet>Fire, but is played well [5]\n- Reviewer treated late-1980s Playin' as a bathroom-break song, unlike this energetic version [5]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **deadandco2016-07-07.akg481**: taped by Jeff Frank; transferred by Jeff Frank; source: AKG 481 > V3 > Marantz PMD661 (16/44.1) [1]\n\n## Art and photos\n\n- Poster by Pine Knob Music Theatre: [Dead And Company Tickets | 7 July 2016 | Pine Knob Music Theatre](https://www.pineknobamp.com/events/dead-and-company/) [7]",
